    "body": "### Problem\n\nI have to use the neovim-releases binaries to run on older systems. This has worked very well until now.\n\nFor v0.12.5, the binary is incorrect and points to a dev version for 0.13, not the v0.12.5.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```bash\nNEOVIM_VERS=\"0.12.5\" wget \"https://github.com/neovim/neovim-releases/releases/download/v$NEOVIM_VERS/nvim-linux-${NEOVIM_ARCH}.tar.gz\"\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nVersion should match the tag.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1410+g510f61555b\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nAlmaLinux 8.10\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nXFCE Terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256-color\n\n### Installation\n\nTarball from neovim/neovim-releases",
